# Keep every text file LF in the working tree on ALL platforms.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true (the GitHub runner
# default) rewrites LF to CRLF on the way out of git, and that breaks the
# byte-exact comparisons: the committed authcontract/authcontract.schema.json
# against its generator, the golden vectors, and anything a POSIX shell
# executes. eol=lf is deliberate rather than `text=auto` alone: auto would
# still hand Windows CRLF. Nothing in this repository needs CRLF.
# (docs/decisions/0073-PLAN-publish-an-auth-contract-module.md, Phase 4)
* text=auto eol=lf
